// CR claude for eric: [bug/high] A read into a union of two abstract types takes the
// first member whose representation accepts the data, and pack writes an abstract value
// bare: `Meters(3.0)` written as `[Meters, Feet]` reads back as `Feet(3.0)`, and the
// type test and `==` then disagree with the value written. json and toml refuse or tag
// such unions (`JsonData`); `Concrete` does not, and sys::net::subscribe, db trees and
// str::parse share the bound (those found by reading). Refuse a union holding an
// abstract type beside a member its data may read as, naming the tagged variant form,
// or carry the tag in pack. probe:
// design/review-2026-11-16/repro/x-traits-abstract-pack-union-of-abstracts.gx
// (x-traits-abstract-02)
/// Decode a value from packed binary bytes.
///
/// To decode from a stream, read it first — `pack::read(Read::read_all(f)?)`.
val read: fn<'b: Concrete>(input: bytes) -> Result<'b, [`PackErr(string), `InvalidCast(string)]>;

/// Encode a value to packed binary bytes, preserving tuple, struct,
/// variant and list kinds. Abstract values write through their Cast impl.
///
/// To write to a stream, write the bytes — `Write::write_exact(f, pack::write_bytes(v)?)`.
val write_bytes: fn<'a: Data>(value: 'a) -> Result<bytes, `PackErr(string)>;
